# Vercel builds the marketing site from `site/` (see vercel.json:
# `cd site && npm ci && npm run build` → `site/dist`). `site/` therefore must NOT
# be excluded — stripping it is what made the build fail with `Missing script:
# "build"` (npm fell through to the root package.json, which has no build script).
# Everything else the build does not need stays excluded to keep the upload small.
/warden/
/analytics/
/grafana/
/postgres/
/redis/
/dashboard/
/portal/
/packages/
/scripts/
/docs/
/skills/
/.agents/
/.claude/
/.github/
/docker/
/protocols/
/obsidian-plugin/
/memory/
/workflows/
*.md

# …except the markdown the site *serves*. `Accept: text/markdown` on a page URL
# is answered from these files (edge/negotiate.mjs maps route → file), so
# excluding them from the upload would 404 every markdown request.
!/site/public/*.md
!/site/public/.well-known/*.md

# Unlinked static mock that enumerates every secret env var name (ADMIN_KEY,
# WARDEN_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY …) — recon aid, not a real page.
/landing/enterprise-settings.html
